{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3276","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3276","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3276\",\"parent_revision\":\"2d2345d56a9a6e11eeb6d7fa605d03652237b626\",\"root_revision\":\"1fc9dfbc859dab7833fe8c674a1a802f9858a8798761f85444deff93d1daa965\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-28\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`agents/contract-verification.md` line 151 states: \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \u2014 you register no artifact and write no task state.\\\" This assumes a synchronous dispatch model where the caller receives the subagent's final text as a direct return value.\\n\\nObserved during this session while running `/dh:implement-feature` on plan Pd95e593c for #3151: dispatching `dh:contract-verification` via the `Agent` tool returned only an async \\\"Spawned successfully\\\" acknowledgment. The agent completed its analysis and went idle twice (confirmed via `ListAgents`), but no message with actual content was ever delivered back \u2014 only bare `idle_notification` events with no `summary` field, unlike every other subagent dispatched in the same session (impact-analyst, fact-checker, classifier, rtica-assessor, alignment-analyst, groomer, feature-researcher, architect, swarm-task-planner, t0/t1 task agents), all of which reported back with a `summary` field containing real content. Sending the idle agent a direct follow-up question asking it to restate its verdict also produced no reply.\\n\\nThe `Agent` tool's own documentation states: \\\"Your plain text output is NOT visible to other agents \u2014 to communicate, you MUST call [SendMessage].\\\" That is the observed cause: `contract-verification.md`'s instructions never tell the agent to call `SendMessage`; they tell it to just \\\"output\\\" its finding as its response, consistent with a synchronous dispatch model this environment does not use for agent-tool dispatch.\\n\\nImpact: `implement-feature`'s Progress Loop step 4a (post-task contract verification) silently produces no usable result under this environment's async dispatch \u2014 the orchestrator either blocks indefinitely waiting for a message that never arrives, or gives up and has to verify the contract manually (as happened this session), defeating the point of delegating the check.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: this is the same class of gap already fixed for a sibling agent \u2014 `git log` shows a merged commit \\\"fix(development-harness): add SendMessage completion report to impact-analyst (#3249)\\\" that added exactly this kind of completion-report step to `dh:impact-analyst`. `dh:contract-verification` appears to have been missed by that same fix, and other `dh:*` agents dispatched by the same Progress Loop may share the identical gap \u2014 not verified for any agent besides contract-verification in this session.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: possible directions for grooming to evaluate, not requirements \u2014 (1) add an explicit `SendMessage` step to `contract-verification.md`'s Output Format section, mirroring whatever change PR #3249 made to `impact-analyst.md`; (2) audit the other `dh:*` agents invoked by `implement-feature`/`add-new-feature`'s Progress Loop for the same synchronous-response assumption, since any could have the identical gap and it would surface the same way (silent, not an error).\\n\\n**User-provided context** (added during grooming, 2026-08-29): another possible direction for grooming/planning to evaluate, not a requirement \u2014 don't make `dh:contract-verification` (or any sibling agent with the same gap) into a `TeamCreate` teammate just to get a working report-back channel. Keep it a plain background `Agent()` spawn, but have it write its result directly to the backend (e.g. `backlog_groom` on the Concerns section, or `artifact_register`, mirroring how `dh:t0-baseline-capture` reports) instead of relying on a returned value or on `SendMessage(to=\\\"team-lead\\\")` \u2014 there is no team-lead when there is no team.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:53:44.790149Z</sub>\\n\\nHYPOTHESIS: this is the same class of gap already fixed for a sibling agent \u2014 `git log` shows a merged commit \\\"fix(development-harness): add SendMessage completion report to impact-analyst (#3249)\\\" that added exactly this kind of completion-report step to `dh:impact-analyst`. `dh:contract-verification` appears to have been missed by that same fix, and other `dh:*` agents dispatched by the same Progress Loop may share the identical gap \u2014 not verified for any agent besides contract-verification in this session.\\n**VERDICT: VERIFIED (with dispatch-context caveat)**\\n\\n**Claim 1 \u2014 contract-verification.md line ~151**\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Current text reads \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \u2014 you register no artifact and write no task state.\\\"\\nevidence: File read confirms exact text at line 151\\nsource: /plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md:151\\n\\n**Claim 2 \u2014 implement-feature step 4a dispatch**\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Dispatch is via bare Agent() call (not TeamCreate) with subagent_type=\\\"dh:contract-verification\\\"\\nevidence: Code inspection shows naked Agent() call at lines 165-184 with synchronous result expectation\\nsource: /plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md:165-184\\n\\n**Claim 3 \u2014 Commit 11082f0eb removed SendMessage from contract-verification**\\nverdict: VERIFIED\\nclaim: Commit 11082f0eb (2026-08-24) \\\"refactor(development-harness): route agent handoffs through the backend, not SendMessage (#3202)\\\" removed SendMessage reporting from contract-verification\\nevidence: git show confirms removal of \\\"When operating as a **teammate** (spawned via `TeamCreate`), send your completion status...\\\" text\\nsource: Commit 11082f0eb diff of contract-verification.md\\n\\n**Claim 4 \u2014 Commit 43058f345 added SendMessage to impact-analyst**\\nverdict: VERIFIED (BUT NOT DIRECTLY TRANSFERABLE DUE TO DISPATCH-CONTEXT MISMATCH)\\nclaim: Commit 43058f345 (2026-08-27) \\\"fix(development-harness): add SendMessage completion report to impact-analyst (#3249)\\\" added SendMessage to impact-analyst.md\\nevidence: git show confirms addition of SendMessage(to=\\\"team-lead\\\",...) pattern\\nsource: Commit 43058f345 diff of impact-analyst.md\\n\\n**CRITICAL FINDING \u2014 Dispatch Context Mismatch:**\\nThe SendMessage fix pattern is NOT directly transferable because the agents operate in different contexts:\\n- **impact-analyst**: Dispatched via TeamCreate(team_name=\\\"groom-{item-slug}\\\") in groom-backlog-item workflow (TEAM MODE)\\n- **contract-verification**: Dispatched via bare Agent() call in implement-feature step 4a (NON-TEAM MODE)\\n\\nThe SendMessage-to-team-lead pattern works for impact-analyst because it's a teammate. Contract-verification's non-team dispatch context may require a different reporting pattern, and the fix applied to impact-analyst cannot be directly copied to contract-verification.\\n\\n**HYPOTHESIS RESOLUTION:** Partially VERIFIED. The gap exists (both agents have missing completion reporting), but the fix path diverges due to dispatch-context differences. Further investigation needed: does the orchestrator in implement-feature step 4a correctly capture and handle contract-verification's synchronous response?\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-28T14:41:39.625254Z</sub>\\n\\n<details><summary>struck: 2026-08-28T15:05:07.470133Z \u2014 Reassess conditions after Impact Radius expansion and Fact-Check verification</summary>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: fix: contract-verification agent's findings never reach the orchestrator under async subagent dispatch\\nDate: 2026-08-29\\nGoal: Determine why contract-verification's findings never reach the im